1
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:14,740
Tell me the man, Muse —
the man of many turnings,

2
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,310
who was driven wandering far,
once he had sacked

3
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:21,270
Troy’s holy citadel:

4
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:25,350
many were the cities of men he saw,
and he learned their minds,

5
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:28,940
many the griefs he suffered at heart
on the open sea,

6
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,200
striving to win his own life
and his companions’ homecoming.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,730
Even so he could not save them,

8
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:37,420
hard though he strove:

9
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:40,220
they perished by their own recklessness,

10
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:43,430
fools, who ate the cattle
of Helios Hyperion,

11
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:46,130
and the god took from them
their day of homecoming.

12
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:51,550
Begin where you will, goddess, daughter of Zeus —
tell us, too, the tale.

13
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:56,780
By then all the others,
all who had escaped sheer ruin,

14
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:00,140
were home, safely past the war
and past the sea.

15
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:05,640
Him alone — aching for homecoming
and his wife —

16
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:10,920
the queenly nymph Calypso,
shining among goddesses, held back

17
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,880
in her hollow caves,
hungry to make him her husband.

18
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:18,650
But when the year came,
in the wheeling round of seasons,

19
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:24,190
in which the gods had spun the thread
of his return home

20
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:29,050
to Ithaca — not even there
was he free of trials,

21
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:34,370
even among his own.
And the gods pitied him,
